        "id": "assumed-0",
        "kind": "note",
        "text": "Assumed\n- by_operation and request_window_seconds re-read from the run's metrics.jsonl: its result.json was written before they were recorded\n- users traffic steady: the run's phases (burst) are flattened to their average rate\n- users timeoutMs 60000: k6's default request timeout; a journey can set its own\n- users retries 0: LiteTraffic adds none; a journey script could\n- app end-to-end mean 546.526 = p50 x sqrt(1 + cv^2), the mean of a lognormal fit to each operation's p95/p50, weighted by samples; Breakscale's serviceMs is a mean\n- app serviceCv 0.2 (raw fit 0.182, clamped to 0.2..1): a lognormal fit to each operation's p95/p50, weighted by samples; the spread between operations is not included\n- app errorRate was measured at the run's own load, so it may include failures caused by that load\n- app instances 1: the replica count is not visible from outside\n- app queueLimit 64: Breakscale default; the real backlog is unknown\n- app timeoutMs 0 and retries 0: Breakscale defaults (no timeout or retry toward the db)\n- no db node: server capture shows no database container, so database time stays inside app serviceMs\n- app serviceMs 546.526 = the end-to-end mean; an upper bound on the app's own time, because it includes queueing, the network and the database call\n- replicaCount, replicationLagMs, shardCount, shardCapacity and hotKeyFraction (and the client's unused service fields) keep Breakscale's defaults; these node kinds do not use them",
